    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d573-f1" n="83" type="source" xml:id="d573-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Consul at Peiping without covering
                    despatch; received September 23.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d573-f2" n="84" xml:id="d573-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d573-f3" n="85" xml:id="d573-f3-content">
                <p>Mr. Clubb’s two memoranda, dated August 3, on “Relationship of Japanese, and
                    particularly Japanese holdout troops, to Chinese Communist actions in Manchuria”
                    and “Relationship of Koreans and Mongols to Communist movement in Manchuria” not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d573-f4" n="86" xml:id="d573-f4-content">
                <p>Col. David D. Barrett, Assistant Military Attaché in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
